Id: time002w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Fix: Read chronyc sources (timedatectl timesync-status); open UDP 123 or configure servers.
References: chronyc(1), timedatectl(1), ntpctl(8)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

A time synchronisation daemon is running, but the clock is not
synchronised: it has not reached a server, or the ones it reached were
rejected. For chronyd this is chronyc tracking's "Leap status: Not
synchronised"; for OpenNTPD, ntpctl -s status's "clock unsynced"; for
the others (and OpenNTPD when ntpctl does not answer), timedatectl's
NTPSynchronized=no. The clock drifts as if nothing were running.

To find out why, 'chronyc sources -v', 'ntpctl -s peers' or
'timedatectl timesync-status'. Usually the servers are unreachable (a firewall
blocking outgoing UDP port 123, or no DNS), or none is configured
(server or pool lines in chrony.conf, servers or server lines in
OpenNTPD's ntpd.conf, NTP= in timesyncd.conf).
